mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>The core content of the <em>Biopharmaceutical Technology</em> course covers a variety of cutting‑edge biotechnologies, which play a vital role in modern drug research, development and production. At the undergraduate level, biopharmaceutical technology includes genetic engineering, cell engineering, antibody engineering, fermentation engineering and enzyme engineering. Students are expected to understand the background and developmental history of these engineering technologies, be familiar with their technical principles, and master the ability to comprehensively apply these technologies to solve problems arising in the research, development and production of biopharmaceuticals. Meanwhile, students should keep track of the development trends of biotechnology.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
